+ * TCP batch, the linear part of a scatter-gather frame) ends on an 8 byte
+ * boundary, which that driver builds for the Wi-Fi TX DMA limitation by
+ * sliding the headers down by the excess; a descriptor never straddles a 4096
+ * byte boundary of the descriptor memory (read when the rings are allocated);
+ * the IP, UDP and TCP checksums of a batch are all enabled in the TCL command
+ * and the TCP NS flag of its segments is cleared. Read for each frame.
